
  Inglenook installer
  -------------------
  This is a root shell running from RAM. Nothing on any disk is changed until
  you confirm it. The USB stick is only needed while the image is copied.

  To install Inglenook onto a disk of this machine, run:

       inglenook-install

  It finds the image on the stick, shows you each disk and what is on it, asks
  for the size of the root (the rest of the disk becomes /var), encrypts the
  disk with the TPM, installs, and tells you when to unplug the stick.

  Looking around first:  lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,TRAN,FSTYPE,LABEL
  Tools: gdisk sgdisk cryptsetup systemd-cryptenroll systemd-repart tpm2_*
         mkfs.* nvme skopeo curl git tar zstd lspci ip dig
  Reboot:  systemctl reboot       Nothing is saved on this stick.

